        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "73ccc78a-b188-5f0e-89f5-f7acd2752682",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James A. McIlroy, Frank Arthur Worsley, Ernest Shackleton\n- Places: McIlroy Peak, Weddell Sea, Antarctica, Sandefjord, Norway\n- Organizations: UK Antarctic Place-Names Committee\n- Expeditions: British Imperial Trans-Antarctic Expedition, Shackleton–Rowett Expedition, Imperial Trans-Antarctic Expedition\n- Ships: Endurance, Quest\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Arthur Worsley was born on 22 February 1872 and died on 1 February 1943.\n- Endurance was launched in 1912 from Sandefjord in Norway.\n- James A. McIlroy served as a surgeon on the British Imperial Trans-Antarctic Expedition of 1914–1916 aboard Endurance.\n- Frank Arthur Worsley was a New Zealand sailor and explorer who served as captain of Endurance on Ernest Shackleton's Imperial Trans-Antarctic Expedition of 1914–1916.\n- Endurance was crushed by ice and sank in the Weddell Sea off Antarctica in 1915, three years after her launch.\n- James A. McIlroy served on the Shackleton–Rowett Expedition of 1921–1922 aboard Quest.\n- McIlroy Peak was named in 1990 by the UK Antarctic Place-Names Committee after Dr. James A. McIlroy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b4811e3f-5439-5751-8ac8-d2330f634fdf",
        "text": "Page: McIlroy Peak. Sentence: It was named by the UK Antarctic Place-Names Committee in 1990 after Dr. James A. McIlroy, surgeon on the British Imperial Trans-Antarctic Expedition, 1914–16, in the \"Endurance\", and on the Shackleton–Rowett Expedition, 1921–22, in the \"Quest\".\nPage: Endurance (1912 ship). Sentence: She was launched in 1912 from Sandefjord in Norway and was crushed by ice, causing her to sink three years later in the Weddell Sea off Antarctica.\nPage: Frank Worsley. Sentence: Frank Arthur Worsley {'1': \", '2': \", '3': \", '4': \"} (22 February 1872 – 1 February 1943) was a New Zealand sailor and explorer who served on Ernest Shackleton's Imperial Trans-Antarctic Expedition of 1914–1916, as captain of the \"Endurance\".",
